            <ArticleTitle>Genetics and the variability of treatment response in asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S532-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pharmacogenetics is the study of how genetic differences influence the variability in patients' responses to therapy. Using specific examples in asthma, I will define the concepts of variability in response to therapy in asthma. I will then use the relationship between specific genetic polymorphisms and the response to beta-adrenergic agonists and leukotriene modifiers to illustrate pharmacogenetic interactions and to acquaint the reader with the applicability of these findings to clinical practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
